    {
      "id": "membrane-behavior",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Behavior",
      "position": {
        "x": -180,
        "y": 80
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "title": "Behavior",
        "body": "## Implemented behavior\n\nmembraneChain traverses the authored chain; membraneGeometry derives the outline. validateGraphInvariants reports MEMBRANE_CHAIN_INCOMPLETE. graphWorkspace resizeGraphMembrane stores explicit bounds, and activeFrameClip computes the internal clip. Workspace layout uses the resulting frame rather than semantic-level screen-size substitutions.\n\n## Known gaps\n\nThe spec records the current clipping and resize contract; drag behavior and custom curved boundaries still need browser evidence beyond geometry unit tests. Authored control-node examples are linked separately from the spec.\n\n## Open decisions\n\nNo additional decision is required to describe the behavior above. Changes to that contract require an explicit task; implementation gaps are not implied approvals.\n\n## Evidence\n\nSource (twilite repository):\n- `components/NodeGraph/membraneChain.js`\n- `components/NodeGraph/membraneGeometry.js`\n- `components/GraphEditor/utils/graphWorkspace.js`\n- `components/GraphEditor/validators/validateGraphInvariants.js`\n\nFocused tests (twilite repository):\n- `tests/membraneGeometry.test.js`\n- `tests/graphWorkspace.test.js`\n- `tests/workspaceCamera.test.js`\n\nThese pointers identify evidence to inspect. Structural validation does not prove runtime or browser behavior.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "definitionKey": "page-section",
